    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "I implemented `build_client` in `app/llm_client.py`, and all 3 tests pass with `pytest -q`. No dependencies were added. It meets the four requirements:\n\n1. **Timeouts:** connect is 5 seconds; read, write and pool are 30 seconds. I set this on both the OpenAI client and its HTTP client. That matters because the OpenAI client sends its own timeout with every request, and it would otherwise override the HTTP client's setting with its default.\n2. **Retries:** `max_retries=2`.\n3. **Logging:** a request event hook on the HTTP client logs `\"<METHOD> <URL>\"` at INFO level on the `app.http` logger. The hook runs on every send, so retries are logged too.\n4. **Transport:** when `transport` is given, the HTTP client uses it. I built the HTTP client with the OpenAI library's own `DefaultHttpxClient`, so it keeps the library's usual connection limits and redirect behaviour.\n\nI also added `tests/test_llm_client.py`, which covers:\n- The timeout values and `max_retries`.\n- A stub transport that fails twice and then succeeds. The test checks that all 3 attempts go through the stub and that each one is logged exactly as `GET https://api.openai.com/v1/models`.\n\nThe retry test skips the wait between retries so it runs quickly."
